Bottom Caption

Institutional Operating System Principle

Governance creates direction.

Finance allocates resources.

Procurement converts resources into capability.

Digital Public Infrastructure enables interoperability.

Institutional Memory preserves learning.

Coordination aligns institutions.

Capability drives execution.

Execution creates competitiveness.

Learning continuously improves the operating system.

Design Style

Use:

White background
Navy blue boxes
Thin gray connectors
Sans-serif font (Inter or IBM Plex Sans)
Consistent spacing
Minimal visual clutter

This should resemble a World Bank or OECD institutional architecture rather than a marketing graphic.
